    narr:narration """This position frames a deployment gate as an already-enforced operational standard, not a proposal under debate. On 2026-07-25, Quinton Fairweather stated in his own voice that [every Meridian deployment now requires a signed release manifest before it ships](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_2), carrying the decision with activated-negative affect and legitimate authority footing. Xena Expertgh then codified the decision into structured bullets under a [key-decisions header](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_4): the [gate itself](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_5), its [scope across staging and production](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_6), and [named ownership](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_7) assigned to Quinton Fairweather. The children collectively present the gate as a ratified fact — concrete, realis, present-tense, decision-conviction throughout — rather than something being argued for. The register is uniformly technical and short-punchy; power reads as legitimate authority, not positional assertion. There is no dissenting child, no qualifier, no 'pending' or 'proposed' hedge anywhere in the set.""" ;
